1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:04,299
Kabir posted in the office group—
"I got laid off today."

2
00:00:04,299 --> 00:00:05,989
Seen by 23…

3
00:00:05,989 --> 00:00:07,069
in his worst week…

4
00:00:07,069 --> 00:00:08,939
replies: zero.

5
00:00:09,139 --> 00:00:12,980
Till yesterday they said— "Bro,
you're one of us!"

6
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:17,382
When friends leave in bad times…
what do you do?

7
00:00:17,592 --> 00:00:19,022
In the Bhagavata Purana…

8
00:00:19,022 --> 00:00:22,628
Gajendra, king of elephants, was
in a lake with his herd.

9
00:00:22,828 --> 00:00:24,098
Then, in the water…

10
00:00:24,098 --> 00:00:26,294
a crocodile seized his leg.

11
00:00:26,814 --> 00:00:28,194
The herd pulled…

12
00:00:28,194 --> 00:00:30,684
but couldn't free him.
The fight went on…

13
00:00:30,684 --> 00:00:32,367
a thousand years.

14
00:00:32,637 --> 00:00:36,157
"My own kin cannot
free me in my distress…

15
00:00:36,157 --> 00:00:39,373
"

16
00:00:39,403 --> 00:00:43,343
"…

17
00:00:43,343 --> 00:00:46,020
so I go to Him, the
supreme refuge."

18
00:00:46,990 --> 00:00:53,732
Meaning: "My own can't free me… so
I go to Him." Parāyaṇam…

19
00:00:53,732 --> 00:00:55,988
the last refuge.

20
00:00:56,008 --> 00:00:58,688
Gajendra blamed no one…

21
00:00:58,688 --> 00:01:00,478
he lifted a lotus…

22
00:01:00,478 --> 00:01:02,095
and Narayana came.

23
00:01:02,195 --> 00:01:04,015
Kabir muted the group…

24
00:01:04,015 --> 00:01:06,365
and made one call. Papa said—

25
00:01:06,365 --> 00:01:08,011
"Come home, son."

26
00:01:08,571 --> 00:01:10,481
Crowds are for good days…

27
00:01:10,481 --> 00:01:13,381
in bad days, one call is enough.

28
00:01:13,651 --> 00:01:17,563
In your bad times… did the group
show up, or one person?

29
00:01:17,563 --> 00:01:20,408
Send this to the
friend who called.
